    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Growing up in the desert, I knew that water was hard to come by. Sadly, we humans are only making the global water shortage worse. During my college years, I felt bad about myself because I was using as much water as everyone else."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A guest lecture in college turned things around for me. For the first time, I learnt about rainwater and greywater harvesting. I decided to give it a go."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I’ve lived in the desert community of Tucson, Arizona, for 30 years. During the monsoon season, more water than we need falls from the sky. But we just let it run off. At the same time, we import water from the Colorado River, 300 miles away, and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pump",
            "zh": "输送"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it uphill 3,000 feet, using a lot of energy and money. It makes me think: Why are we wasting all this energy when there’s already plenty of rainwater here?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I started small. I dug out "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "basin-shaped",
            "zh": "盆状的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " garden beds with a raised path beside them. As rain hits the path, it flows into the garden, watering the plants. I then set up a tank to collect rainwater from the house roof for use in the garden during dry times."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I also thought about how I could reuse greywater. I started with my washing machine. At the back, there is a pipe that sends the used water to the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sewer",
            "zh": "污水管"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". I added another pipe. Every time I wash my clothes, the water flows out to my garden and waters the trees."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "With these set-ups, 95 per cent of the water I use to water my garden comes from free on-site sources. Our family of four now uses less than 20 gallons of city water per person per day. For comparison, the average American uses five times more! I’m saving a lot of money on my water bills. My plants are also living a better life. They look much greener and healthier because rainwater and greywater don’t contain "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "chlorine",
            "zh": "氯"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "I’m always trying to improve my set-ups. At the same time, I’m sharing my experience with my neighbours. I want more people to see how satisfying it is to be part of the solution, not the problem."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
